(1835777, 248361, 45844, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments! I learned a lot with this image.<br/> <br/>In retrospect, I agree with those of you who said it''s too dark. I wanted the picture to have a warm feel, but lost clarity in doing that. And since spot editing wasn''t allowed, I couldn''t use <a href="//photos.viking054.com/archives/2005/11/000226large.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this other version</a>, which I think works better.</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments! I learned a lot with this image. In retrospect, I agree with those of you who said it''s too dark. I wanted the picture to have a warm feel, but lost clarity in doing that. And since spot editing wasn''t allowed, I couldn''t use this other version, which I think works better.', '2005-11-03 11:40:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1836184, 248823, 12253, '<td valign="top">I agree with Ursula that this scored way too low.  It''s a nice image, good movement abstraction.  I would however, have preferred it without most of the stem--a crop of the left portion just above the leaf.  The danger of that is that it does appear to be "severed" and "floating", but I find the blur effect on the stem, especially the leaf, more a distraction than anything else.  Worth playing with some crops.  Don''t let the DPC voters discourage you from experimenting like this!</td>', 'I agree with Ursula that this scored way too low.  It''s a nice image, good movement abstraction.  I would however, have preferred it without most of the stem--a crop of the left portion just above the leaf.  The danger of that is that it does appear to be "severed" and "floating", but I find the blur effect on the stem, especially the leaf, more a distraction than anything else.  Worth playing with some crops.  Don''t let the DPC voters discourage you from experimenting like this!', '2005-11-03 15:10:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1836189, 248600, 12253, '<td valign="top">Sorry the DPC voters treated this nice shot so roughly!  Don''t let it discourage you! One post comment: you might try a crop at the top--the black/yellow vertical divider does not contribute to the image.</td>', 'Sorry the DPC voters treated this nice shot so roughly!  Don''t let it discourage you! One post comment: you might try a crop at the top--the black/yellow vertical divider does not contribute to the image.', '2005-11-03 15:12:36.000000', NULL, 0),
